@startuml fig-3-6-freshness-state-machine
' Figure 3.6: freshness state machine. Freshness is separate from lifecycle, evidence status and user relevance.
' Transition reasons match freshness_transitions (migrations 024, 034) and freshness-transition-policy.ts.
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
  ArrowColor black
}

title Figure 3.6 - Freshness state machine (current, needs_update, expired)

state "current" as current
state "needs_update" as needs_update
state "expired" as expired

[*] --> current : version published\n(starts current)

current --> needs_update : review_due_at passed\n(review_deadline_missed)
current --> needs_update : source report retracted,\nsuperseded or withdrawn\n(live dataset)
current --> expired : issuer valid_until reached\n(issuer_validity_ended)
needs_update --> expired : issuer valid_until reached\n(issuer_validity_ended)
needs_update --> current : new applicable evidence\nevaluated
expired --> current : new applicable evidence\nevaluated

note right of expired
  Only the issuer's validity window
  sets expired. Expired never means
  resolved, safe or no longer relevant.
end note

note bottom of needs_update
  A passed review deadline or withdrawn
  support. It does not prove the event ended.
end note

@enduml
